Sat Oct 10 11:14:44 UTC 2026 - Tina Müller <timueller+perl@suse.de>

- updated to 1.70.0 (1.07)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-ExtUtils-Typemaps-Default/Changes

  1.07   Fri Oct  9 CET 2026
    - Address CVE-2026-107794:
      Fix integer underflow in ExtUtils::Typemaps::STL::List on empty lists.
      Calling av_extend(av, len-1) when len == 0 underflowed the unsigned
      integer and attempted to allocate a 32GiB array.
    - Fix missing index increment in std::list<char*> OUTPUT typemaps.

  1.06   Thu Oct  8 CET 2026
    - Address CVE-2026-107373:
      Using "std::string( SvPV_nolen( $arg ), SvCUR( $arg ) );"
      adds a potential security issue since in C++ the evaluation of argument
      order depends on the compiler.  If the SV is not stringified (for
      example, if it's an IV, NV or a reference) then this can abort or segfault.
      The fix applied is to split into multiple statements:
       STRLEN len;
       const char *pv = SvPV($arg, len);
       $var = std::string(pv, len);

      If you depend on this module, please update your minimum version
      requirement to 1.06.
    - Do not depend on dev release version of ExtUtils::Typemaps anymore.
    - Updated author contact info.

